---
title: Spaghetti alla puttanesca
servings: 4
tags: [italian, quick, weeknight]
cuisine: italian
time: 40 minutes
source: Spaghetti alla puttanesca by GialloZafferano, https://www.giallozafferano.com/recipes/Spaghetti-alla-puttanesca.html
---

Rinse the @capers{10%g}(salted) well, pat dry and chop roughly. Crush the
@black olives{100%g}(Gaeta, pitted) under the flat of a knife. Chop the
@parsley{1%bunch}.

Put a #large pot{} of water on to boil and salt it.

In a #large frying pan{}, put the @olive oil{2.5%tbsp}(extra virgin), the
@garlic{3%cloves}(peeled, whole), the @dried chilies{2}(chopped), the
@anchovies{25%g}(in oil) and the capers. Cook over medium heat ~{5%minutes},
stirring, until the anchovies melt.

Mash the @whole peeled tomatoes{800%g} a little, add them, and cook over medium
heat ~{10%minutes}.

Meanwhile cook the @dried pasta{320%g}(spaghetti) until al dente.

Fish out the garlic. Stir the olives and parsley into the sauce. Drain the
spaghetti into the pan, toss ~{30%seconds}, and serve at once.

> Anchovies, capers and olives bring plenty of salt; taste before adding any.
